UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Charcoal metal faces and a neutral-white rear halo create a clear identity on a deep teal wall. A pale stone desk and side daylight give the reception a lighter, more contemporary character.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Send a straight-on wall photo and the desk and wall dimensions.

### Light, material and identity

Compare warm, neutral or cool white against the wall and surrounding lighting. Agree the actual light colour for your order.

### Make the proportions work

Wall texture, stand-off distance and letter spacing affect light spread. Resolve cable exits, driver location and maintenance access before the wall is finished.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Office & reception

**Construction direction:** Opaque metal face with dimensional returns

**Lighting:** Rear LED halo; light colour to be agreed

**Finish direction:** Neutral-white halo · Teal reception wall

**Mounting approach:** Stand-off fixing with concealed cable exits

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Charcoal metal faces and a neutral-white rear halo create a clear identity on a deep teal wall. A pale stone desk and side daylight give the reception a lighter, more contemporary character.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Send a straight-on wall photo and the desk and wall dimensions.

### Light, material and identity

Compare warm, neutral or cool white against the wall and surrounding lighting. Agree the actual light colour for your order.

### Make the proportions work

Wall texture, stand-off distance and letter spacing affect light spread. Resolve cable exits, driver location and maintenance access before the wall is finished.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Office & reception

**Construction direction:** Opaque metal face with dimensional returns

**Lighting:** Rear LED halo; light colour to be agreed

**Finish direction:** Neutral-white halo · Teal reception wall

**Mounting approach:** Stand-off fixing with concealed cable exits

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='office-logo-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nCreate a recognisable arrival point without overpowering the interior. This reception concept pairs a dimensional logo with soft rear illumination, leaving space around the mark so it reads clearly from the entrance.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Light behind the logo\n\nRear illumination outlines the lettering while keeping the faces visually calm. Wall texture and stand-off distance affect how the halo spreads.\n\n### Finish in conversation with the space\n\nA warm metal appearance works with stone and timber. The final metal, surface treatment and colour reference are selected for your brand.\n\n### Scale around the reception desk\n\nUse the desk width, wall area and entrance sightline to set the overall logo width and position. A wall photograph is more useful than a letter height alone.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Office and reception feature wall\n\n**Letter construction:** Opaque metal face and formed returns; construction to be specified\n\n**Lighting direction:** Rear LED illumination; warm or neutral white to be reviewed\n\n**Finish:** Brushed, painted or plated appearance by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stand-off fixing with a planned cable route behind the sign\n\n**Size & scope:** Made to your artwork; dimensions, components and installation scope quoted individually\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Check the wall\n\nSend a straight-on photo, available width and height, and wall material. Uneven or reflective finishes can change the halo.\n\n### Plan power and access\n\nIdentify the cable exit, driver location and maintenance access with your installer before the wall is closed.\n\n### Review the visual proof\n\nConfirm logo spacing, wall clearance, light colour and the sign position on your wall drawing before production.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nReplace the mark and lettering with your own vector artwork. Adjust the overall scale, metal finish and light colour to suit the space.\n\nFor multiple reception locations, share a wall photo and dimensions for each site so the same visual direction can be adapted consistently."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nCreate a recognisable arrival point without overpowering the interior. This reception concept pairs a dimensional logo with soft rear illumination, leaving space around the mark so it reads clearly from the entrance.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Light behind the logo\n\nRear illumination outlines the lettering while keeping the faces visually calm. Wall texture and stand-off distance affect how the halo spreads.\n\n### Finish in conversation with the space\n\nA warm metal appearance works with stone and timber. The final metal, surface treatment and colour reference are selected for your brand.\n\n### Scale around the reception desk\n\nUse the desk width, wall area and entrance sightline to set the overall logo width and position. A wall photograph is more useful than a letter height alone.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Office and reception feature wall\n\n**Letter construction:** Opaque metal face and formed returns; construction to be specified\n\n**Lighting direction:** Rear LED illumination; warm or neutral white to be reviewed\n\n**Finish:** Brushed, painted or plated appearance by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stand-off fixing with a planned cable route behind the sign\n\n**Size & scope:** Made to your artwork; dimensions, components and installation scope quoted individually\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Check the wall\n\nSend a straight-on photo, available width and height, and wall material. Uneven or reflective finishes can change the halo.\n\n### Plan power and access\n\nIdentify the cable exit, driver location and maintenance access with your installer before the wall is closed.\n\n### Review the visual proof\n\nConfirm logo spacing, wall clearance, light colour and the sign position on your wall drawing before production.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nReplace the mark and lettering with your own vector artwork. Adjust the overall scale, metal finish and light colour to suit the space.\n\nFor multiple reception locations, share a wall photo and dimensions for each site so the same visual direction can be adapted consistently."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
