reference · Halo-Lit Letter Construction"}],"references":[],"tags":["Warm light","Low-light interior"],"body":"## The Design Brief\n\nWarm rear illumination works with darker finishes and low ambient light. The letter spacing keeps the wording readable while the halo adds depth.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Designed for the setting\n\nReview brightness and mounting distance in relation to the surrounding lighting.\n\n### Light, material and identity\n\nCompare warm, neutral or cool white against the wall and surrounding lighting. Agree the actual light colour for your order.\n\n### Make the proportions work\n\nWall texture, stand-off distance and letter spacing affect light spread. Resolve cable exits, driver location and maintenance access before the wall is finished.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Dining & hospitality\n\n**Construction direction:** Opaque metal face with dimensional returns\n\n**Lighting:** Rear LED halo; light colour to be agreed\n\n**Finish direction:** Warm light · Low-light interior\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stand-off fixing with concealed cable exits\n\n**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site","sourceNote":"AI-generated illustrative design concept; not a delivered customer project. Original asset provenance is recorded in the project media ledgers."}','published',18);
