UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

White and teal illuminated letter faces give a pale stone frontage a distinct identity. The separate cross symbol and secondary wording establish a clear hierarchy.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Send the full frontage width, logo artwork and a straight-on site photo.

### Light, material and identity

The light-transmitting face and formed side work as one letter. Review the face colour, depth, edges and the smallest artwork details.

### Make the proportions work

Identify the substrate, any carrier or raceway requirement, cable penetrations and access for the power supply. Site and destination requirements must be agreed.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Clinic frontage

**Construction direction:** Individual channel letters with light-transmitting faces

**Lighting:** Internal LED face illumination

**Finish direction:** Front-lit letters · Clinic identity

**Mounting approach:** Direct, stand-off or raceway fixing to be reviewed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

White and teal illuminated letter faces give a pale stone frontage a distinct identity. The separate cross symbol and secondary wording establish a clear hierarchy.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Send the full frontage width, logo artwork and a straight-on site photo.

### Light, material and identity

The light-transmitting face and formed side work as one letter. Review the face colour, depth, edges and the smallest artwork details.

### Make the proportions work

Identify the substrate, any carrier or raceway requirement, cable penetrations and access for the power supply. Site and destination requirements must be agreed.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Clinic frontage

**Construction direction:** Individual channel letters with light-transmitting faces

**Lighting:** Internal LED face illumination

**Finish direction:** Front-lit letters · Clinic identity

**Mounting approach:** Direct, stand-off or raceway fixing to be reviewed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='storefront-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nMake the business name easy to identify above the entrance. This storefront concept uses individual illuminated letters on a dark fascia, with generous spacing and a clear relationship to the door and glazing below.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### A clear illuminated face\n\nThe face carries the light, helping the lettering stand apart from the darker fascia. Brightness and colour need to suit the surroundings.\n\n### Letters that fit the frontage\n\nThe sign sits within the architectural band rather than filling every available edge. Review viewing distance and landlord restrictions when setting the size.\n\n### Concealed details\n\nFixings and cable routes should be planned with the fascia construction. Discuss individual mounting or a carrier where access is limited.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Shopfront or commercial fascia\n\n**Letter construction:** Light-transmitting face with formed returns; material to be agreed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Front-facing LED illumination\n\n**Finish:** Face colour and return finish matched to an approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Individual fixings or a carrier, selected for the fascia\n\n**Size & scope:** Logo, overall width and quantities confirmed from your frontage measurements\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Survey the fascia\n\nProvide the sign area, surface material, viewing distance and a straight-on site photo.\n\n### Confirm site requirements\n\nIdentify property approvals, local sign rules and destination electrical requirements with the responsible local team.\n\n### Coordinate the connection\n\nPlan cable penetrations, driver access and weather exposure before fabrication and local installation.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nUse your own logotype and colour palette. Compare face illumination, letter depth and return finish against the façade.\n\nFor more than one shop, identify the quantities, sign sizes and destination for each location in your enquiry."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nMake the business name easy to identify above the entrance. This storefront concept uses individual illuminated letters on a dark fascia, with generous spacing and a clear relationship to the door and glazing below.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### A clear illuminated face\n\nThe face carries the light, helping the lettering stand apart from the darker fascia. Brightness and colour need to suit the surroundings.\n\n### Letters that fit the frontage\n\nThe sign sits within the architectural band rather than filling every available edge. Review viewing distance and landlord restrictions when setting the size.\n\n### Concealed details\n\nFixings and cable routes should be planned with the fascia construction. Discuss individual mounting or a carrier where access is limited.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Shopfront or commercial fascia\n\n**Letter construction:** Light-transmitting face with formed returns; material to be agreed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Front-facing LED illumination\n\n**Finish:** Face colour and return finish matched to an approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Individual fixings or a carrier, selected for the fascia\n\n**Size & scope:** Logo, overall width and quantities confirmed from your frontage measurements\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Survey the fascia\n\nProvide the sign area, surface material, viewing distance and a straight-on site photo.\n\n### Confirm site requirements\n\nIdentify property approvals, local sign rules and destination electrical requirements with the responsible local team.\n\n### Coordinate the connection\n\nPlan cable penetrations, driver access and weather exposure before fabrication and local installation.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nUse your own logotype and colour palette. Compare face illumination, letter depth and return finish against the façade.\n\nFor more than one shop, identify the quantities, sign sizes and destination for each location in your enquiry."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
