UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

A simple crest and serif lettering use material and dimensional edges for character. Ambient light reveals the brushed surface without integral lighting.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Identify the site exposure and approve a real finish reference where required.

### Light, material and identity

Artwork and required depth guide the choice between cut material and a formed dimensional construction. Small strokes and fixing details need review at size.

### Make the proportions work

Unlit letters depend on daylight or site lighting. Review wall clearance, stud positions and attachment to the actual wall or cladding with your installer.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Hospitality entrance

**Construction direction:** Dimensional or cut metal lettering

**Lighting:** Non-illuminated; natural light and cast shadow

**Finish direction:** Bronze appearance · Unlit lettering

**Mounting approach:** Pin or stud fixing suited to the substrate

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

A simple crest and serif lettering use material and dimensional edges for character. Ambient light reveals the brushed surface without integral lighting.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Identify the site exposure and approve a real finish reference where required.

### Light, material and identity

Artwork and required depth guide the choice between cut material and a formed dimensional construction. Small strokes and fixing details need review at size.

### Make the proportions work

Unlit letters depend on daylight or site lighting. Review wall clearance, stud positions and attachment to the actual wall or cladding with your installer.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Hospitality entrance

**Construction direction:** Dimensional or cut metal lettering

**Lighting:** Non-illuminated; natural light and cast shadow

**Finish direction:** Bronze appearance · Unlit lettering

**Mounting approach:** Pin or stud fixing suited to the substrate

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='hospitality-metal-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nGive a hospitality entrance an understated identity that belongs to the architecture. This concept uses unlit dimensional lettering, with the material finish and surrounding ambient light doing the visual work.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Material takes the lead\n\nA warm brushed-metal appearance creates contrast against the entrance surface. Discuss real finish references rather than relying on a screen colour.\n\n### Depth without integral lighting\n\nRaised lettering casts a changing shadow. Return depth and fixing position need to be balanced with logo size and the viewing angle.\n\n### Room around the identity\n\nThe name remains one considered element of the entrance. Align the sign with door, cladding and architectural features.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Hotel, hospitality or commercial entrance\n\n**Letter construction:** Cut or built-up metal, selected to suit the artwork and required depth\n\n**Lighting direction:** Unlit lettering; appearance depends on daylight and site lighting\n\n**Finish:** Brushed, painted or plated surface, subject to finish approval\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stud fixing or a backing arrangement suitable for the substrate\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall width, depth, metal grade and exposed environment to be confirmed\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Identify exposure\n\nTell us whether the location is sheltered, fully outdoors or near the coast. This informs the material and finish review.\n\n### Check the substrate\n\nProvide cladding and wall details so your installer can plan suitable fixings and access.\n\n### Review the light\n\nInclude a day and evening site photo. Unlit lettering depends on the lighting already available at the entrance.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nChange the font, symbol, metal appearance and dimensional depth. Share a physical or photographed finish reference where colour matching is important.\n\nCoordinate entrance lettering with room, floor or directional signs by including a schedule of the additional items."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nGive a hospitality entrance an understated identity that belongs to the architecture. This concept uses unlit dimensional lettering, with the material finish and surrounding ambient light doing the visual work.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Material takes the lead\n\nA warm brushed-metal appearance creates contrast against the entrance surface. Discuss real finish references rather than relying on a screen colour.\n\n### Depth without integral lighting\n\nRaised lettering casts a changing shadow. Return depth and fixing position need to be balanced with logo size and the viewing angle.\n\n### Room around the identity\n\nThe name remains one considered element of the entrance. Align the sign with door, cladding and architectural features.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Hotel, hospitality or commercial entrance\n\n**Letter construction:** Cut or built-up metal, selected to suit the artwork and required depth\n\n**Lighting direction:** Unlit lettering; appearance depends on daylight and site lighting\n\n**Finish:** Brushed, painted or plated surface, subject to finish approval\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stud fixing or a backing arrangement suitable for the substrate\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall width, depth, metal grade and exposed environment to be confirmed\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Identify exposure\n\nTell us whether the location is sheltered, fully outdoors or near the coast. This informs the material and finish review.\n\n### Check the substrate\n\nProvide cladding and wall details so your installer can plan suitable fixings and access.\n\n### Review the light\n\nInclude a day and evening site photo. Unlit lettering depends on the lighting already available at the entrance.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nChange the font, symbol, metal appearance and dimensional depth. Share a physical or photographed finish reference where colour matching is important.\n\nCoordinate entrance lettering with room, floor or directional signs by including a schedule of the additional items."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
