mple","caption":"Fabrication reference · Formed Metal Lettering"}],"references":[],"tags":["Surface texture","Natural shadows"],"body":"## The Design Brief\n\nMetal faces and returns catch changing room light. The design can be developed through surface sheen, thickness and the distance from the wall.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Designed for the setting\n\nCompare finish samples under the lighting available at the installation.\n\n### Light, material and identity\n\nArtwork and required depth guide the choice between cut material and a formed dimensional construction. Small strokes and fixing details need review at size.\n\n### Make the proportions work\n\nUnlit letters depend on daylight or site lighting. Review wall clearance, stud positions and attachment to the actual wall or cladding with your installer.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Interior brand wall\n\n**Construction direction:** Dimensional or cut metal lettering\n\n**Lighting:** Non-illuminated; natural light and cast shadow\n\n**Finish direction:** Surface texture · Natural shadows\n\n**Mounting approach:** Pin or stud fixing suited to the substrate\n\n**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site","sourceNote":"AI-generated illustrative design concept; not a delivered customer project. Original asset provenance is recorded in the project media ledgers."}','published',20);
