UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

A saturated single colour turns straightforward lettering into a focal point. The wall and furniture establish scale while daylight defines the depth.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Review the surface sheen, thickness and any restrictions on wall drilling.

### Light, material and identity

Identify opaque, clear and translucent areas in the artwork. Approve the material or painted colour reference rather than relying only on a screen image.

### Make the proportions work

Tell us if drilling is restricted. Studs, adhesives and backing options must be selected for the sign, surface and local installation conditions.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Reception wall

**Construction direction:** Cut or layered acrylic lettering and logo components

**Lighting:** Non-illuminated material appearance

**Finish direction:** Solid colour · Dimensional letters

**Mounting approach:** Wall fixing and component spacing to be resolved

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

A saturated single colour turns straightforward lettering into a focal point. The wall and furniture establish scale while daylight defines the depth.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Review the surface sheen, thickness and any restrictions on wall drilling.

### Light, material and identity

Identify opaque, clear and translucent areas in the artwork. Approve the material or painted colour reference rather than relying only on a screen image.

### Make the proportions work

Tell us if drilling is restricted. Studs, adhesives and backing options must be selected for the sign, surface and local installation conditions.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Reception wall

**Construction direction:** Cut or layered acrylic lettering and logo components

**Lighting:** Non-illuminated material appearance

**Finish direction:** Solid colour · Dimensional letters

**Mounting approach:** Wall fixing and component spacing to be resolved

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='acrylic-reception-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nBring a brand colour into a bright reception space. The concept uses solid-looking dimensional lettering with a clean outline, relying on colour contrast and depth rather than integral lighting.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Brand colour as the focal point\n\nA saturated colour reads against the pale wall. Confirm the colour reference and whether a painted or material colour is required.\n\n### A simple dimensional silhouette\n\nThe artwork should retain clear strokes at the selected size. Review small counters and fine details before agreeing the fabrication approach.\n\n### Daylight and shadow\n\nUnlit lettering uses the room light to reveal depth. The wall and furniture establish the scale of the mark.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Office, studio or reception brand wall\n\n**Letter construction:** Cut or layered acrylic; thickness and assembly to be reviewed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Unlit construction in this concept\n\n**Finish:** Solid colour, surface sheen and edge finish by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stud, adhesive or backing option selected for the wall and letter size\n\n**Size & scope:** Artwork, available wall area and letter thickness confirmed before production\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Measure the usable wall\n\nShare the wall width and height with any sockets, furniture or features that constrain the layout.\n\n### Discuss fixing limits\n\nTell us if drilling is restricted. Your installer should confirm the surface and suitable attachment method.\n\n### Approve colour and outline\n\nSend vector artwork and a colour reference. Review cut details and any proposed layering before fabrication.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nAdapt the logo, letter colour, thickness and surface sheen. Layer different colours or add a backing panel if required by the design.\n\nIf you want illumination, request it explicitly so the material and assembly can be reviewed for that different construction."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nBring a brand colour into a bright reception space. The concept uses solid-looking dimensional lettering with a clean outline, relying on colour contrast and depth rather than integral lighting.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Brand colour as the focal point\n\nA saturated colour reads against the pale wall. Confirm the colour reference and whether a painted or material colour is required.\n\n### A simple dimensional silhouette\n\nThe artwork should retain clear strokes at the selected size. Review small counters and fine details before agreeing the fabrication approach.\n\n### Daylight and shadow\n\nUnlit lettering uses the room light to reveal depth. The wall and furniture establish the scale of the mark.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Office, studio or reception brand wall\n\n**Letter construction:** Cut or layered acrylic; thickness and assembly to be reviewed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Unlit construction in this concept\n\n**Finish:** Solid colour, surface sheen and edge finish by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Stud, adhesive or backing option selected for the wall and letter size\n\n**Size & scope:** Artwork, available wall area and letter thickness confirmed before production\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Measure the usable wall\n\nShare the wall width and height with any sockets, furniture or features that constrain the layout.\n\n### Discuss fixing limits\n\nTell us if drilling is restricted. Your installer should confirm the surface and suitable attachment method.\n\n### Approve colour and outline\n\nSend vector artwork and a colour reference. Review cut details and any proposed layering before fabrication.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nAdapt the logo, letter colour, thickness and surface sheen. Layer different colours or add a backing panel if required by the design.\n\nIf you want illumination, request it explicitly so the material and assembly can be reviewed for that different construction."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
