UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.intro','Warm illuminated script sits within the glazing while preserving views into the space. Reflections and the background affect how the sign reads.'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.intro','Warm illuminated script sits within the glazing while preserving views into the space. Reflections and the background affect how the sign reads.'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='cafe-neon-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.intro'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"A continuous illuminated line creates an inviting focal point in a café window."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.intro'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"A continuous illuminated line creates an inviting focal point in a café window."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Warm illuminated script sits within the glazing while preserving views into the space. Reflections and the background affect how the sign reads.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Provide the window dimensions and the proposed hanging or fixing points.

### Light, material and identity

A lightbox displays graphics through a lit face. A neon-style sign follows the strokes in the artwork. These effects use different construction approaches.

### Make the proportions work

Confirm cable exit, accessible power-supply location and indoor or outdoor use. Any dimming, control or documentation requirement belongs in the quoted configuration.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Interior shop window

**Construction direction:** Cabinet/lightbox or flexible illuminated line construction

**Lighting:** Flexible neon-style illuminated strokes

**Finish direction:** Warm line effect · Window installation

**Mounting approach:** Wall, projecting or suspended arrangement to be reviewed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Warm illuminated script sits within the glazing while preserving views into the space. Reflections and the background affect how the sign reads.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Provide the window dimensions and the proposed hanging or fixing points.

### Light, material and identity

A lightbox displays graphics through a lit face. A neon-style sign follows the strokes in the artwork. These effects use different construction approaches.

### Make the proportions work

Confirm cable exit, accessible power-supply location and indoor or outdoor use. Any dimming, control or documentation requirement belongs in the quoted configuration.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Interior shop window

**Construction direction:** Cabinet/lightbox or flexible illuminated line construction

**Lighting:** Flexible neon-style illuminated strokes

**Finish direction:** Warm line effect · Window installation

**Mounting approach:** Wall, projecting or suspended arrangement to be reviewed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='cafe-neon-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nCreate a warm window accent that can be seen from the pavement while preserving the view into the café. This concept uses script-style illuminated lines on a clear backing, positioned above the customer seating area.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### A continuous line of light\n\nA line-based word or logo suits a neon-style approach. Tight bends, small lettering and stroke spacing need a construction review.\n\n### A backing that stays quiet\n\nA clear backing keeps the window visually open. Discuss its outline, visible fixing points and how the cable will leave the sign.\n\n### Place it within the window\n\nBalance the sign with the glazing, reflections and customer sightlines. The concept is an interior window application.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Interior café, restaurant or shop window\n\n**Sign construction:** Neon-style LED line on a backing; exact system to be agreed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Visible illuminated line; light colour and control options to discuss\n\n**Backing:** Clear, shaped or coloured panel by approved drawing\n\n**Mounting approach:** Hanging or fixed arrangement suited to the window area\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall size, minimum detail, cable exit and power arrangement quoted for your artwork\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Record the window dimensions\n\nInclude the clear opening, mullions and the position where the sign can hang or fix.\n\n### Plan the supply cable\n\nIdentify a power point, cable route and accessible power-supply position. Avoid assuming the illustration defines the electrical scope.\n\n### Review the artwork\n\nSend your wording or vector logo and preferred light colour. We review line paths, bends and backing shape before approval.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nReplace the wording with your own message or logo. Explore light colours, backing shapes and the arrangement of separate illuminated sections.\n\nFor a projecting lightbox or outdoor location, specify the different application so the enclosure, fixing and exposure can be reviewed."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nCreate a warm window accent that can be seen from the pavement while preserving the view into the café. This concept uses script-style illuminated lines on a clear backing, positioned above the customer seating area.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### A continuous line of light\n\nA line-based word or logo suits a neon-style approach. Tight bends, small lettering and stroke spacing need a construction review.\n\n### A backing that stays quiet\n\nA clear backing keeps the window visually open. Discuss its outline, visible fixing points and how the cable will leave the sign.\n\n### Place it within the window\n\nBalance the sign with the glazing, reflections and customer sightlines. The concept is an interior window application.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Interior café, restaurant or shop window\n\n**Sign construction:** Neon-style LED line on a backing; exact system to be agreed\n\n**Lighting direction:** Visible illuminated line; light colour and control options to discuss\n\n**Backing:** Clear, shaped or coloured panel by approved drawing\n\n**Mounting approach:** Hanging or fixed arrangement suited to the window area\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall size, minimum detail, cable exit and power arrangement quoted for your artwork\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Record the window dimensions\n\nInclude the clear opening, mullions and the position where the sign can hang or fix.\n\n### Plan the supply cable\n\nIdentify a power point, cable route and accessible power-supply position. Avoid assuming the illustration defines the electrical scope.\n\n### Review the artwork\n\nSend your wording or vector logo and preferred light colour. We review line paths, bends and backing shape before approval.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nReplace the wording with your own message or logo. Explore light colours, backing shapes and the arrangement of separate illuminated sections.\n\nFor a projecting lightbox or outdoor location, specify the different application so the enclosure, fixing and exposure can be reviewed."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
