UPDATE content_items SET draft_json=json_set(draft_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Warm visible lights bring character to deep dimensional letters. The building façade provides the scale and frame for the lettering.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Tell us the destination, exposure and intended maintenance access.

### Light, material and identity

Start with artwork or a reference and identify which parts need depth, illumination or a particular surface. The drawing must define the proposed combination.

### Make the proportions work

Review overall size, fixing, electrical arrangement, exposure and destination requirements. Approve the drawings and required components before production.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Dining & hospitality

**Construction direction:** Custom dimensional lettering or mixed-material logo

**Lighting:** Exposed light points or the illustrated lighting direction

**Finish direction:** Warm light points · Deep lettering

**Mounting approach:** Custom mounting and wiring layout to be agreed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),published_json=json_set(published_json,'$.body','## The Design Brief

Warm visible lights bring character to deep dimensional letters. The building façade provides the scale and frame for the lettering.

## Design Decisions

### Designed for the setting

Tell us the destination, exposure and intended maintenance access.

### Light, material and identity

Start with artwork or a reference and identify which parts need depth, illumination or a particular surface. The drawing must define the proposed combination.

### Make the proportions work

Review overall size, fixing, electrical arrangement, exposure and destination requirements. Approve the drawings and required components before production.

## Proposed Configuration

**Application:** Dining & hospitality

**Construction direction:** Custom dimensional lettering or mixed-material logo

**Lighting:** Exposed light points or the illustrated lighting direction

**Finish direction:** Warm light points · Deep lettering

**Mounting approach:** Custom mounting and wiring layout to be agreed

**Size & supply scope:** Custom dimensions, components and delivery quoted around your artwork and site'),version=version+1 WHERE type='project' AND slug='marquee-entrance-concept' AND status='published' AND replace(json_extract(draft_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nGive a restaurant or entertainment entrance a strong evening identity. This concept combines deep dimensional lettering with visible points of light, using the entrance architecture as a frame.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Light points as part of the identity\n\nThe visible lighting rhythm gives the letters their character. Point size, spacing and the artwork need to be designed together.\n\n### Depth and finish add presence\n\nThe metal appearance and returns create a substantial silhouette in daylight as well as at night. Confirm the actual material and finish separately.\n\n### Coordinate with the entrance\n\nReview the wall space above the door, adjacent light fittings and the sign viewing angle before setting the final layout.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Restaurant, bar or entertainment entrance\n\n**Letter construction:** Built-up dimensional letters; construction developed around the design\n\n**Lighting direction:** Exposed light points; component type and spacing to be specified\n\n**Finish:** Painted or metal appearance by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Individual or supported mounting, reviewed against the structure\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall width, return depth, light-point arrangement and access confirmed before quoting\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Check fixing and access\n\nIdentify the wall construction and how the installer will reach and maintain the sign.\n\n### Review exposure and components\n\nTell us the destination and whether the sign is exposed to rain. Component selection and required documentation must suit the agreed configuration.\n\n### Confirm the light pattern\n\nApprove a drawing showing letter profiles and light-point positions, together with the finish and cable arrangement.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nChange the lettering, finish and light-point arrangement. The design can be adapted for a smaller interior feature or a larger entrance identity.\n\nInclude any dimming, replacement-access or event-use requirements at the enquiry stage so they can be reviewed in the quotation."}','$.v'),char(13),'') AND replace(json_extract(published_json,'$.body'),char(13),'')=replace(json_extract('{"v":"## The Design Brief\n\nGive a restaurant or entertainment entrance a strong evening identity. This concept combines deep dimensional lettering with visible points of light, using the entrance architecture as a frame.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Light points as part of the identity\n\nThe visible lighting rhythm gives the letters their character. Point size, spacing and the artwork need to be designed together.\n\n### Depth and finish add presence\n\nThe metal appearance and returns create a substantial silhouette in daylight as well as at night. Confirm the actual material and finish separately.\n\n### Coordinate with the entrance\n\nReview the wall space above the door, adjacent light fittings and the sign viewing angle before setting the final layout.\n\n## Proposed Configuration\n\n**Application:** Restaurant, bar or entertainment entrance\n\n**Letter construction:** Built-up dimensional letters; construction developed around the design\n\n**Lighting direction:** Exposed light points; component type and spacing to be specified\n\n**Finish:** Painted or metal appearance by approved reference\n\n**Mounting approach:** Individual or supported mounting, reviewed against the structure\n\n**Size & scope:** Overall width, return depth, light-point arrangement and access confirmed before quoting\n\n## Prepare Your Installation\n\n### Check fixing and access\n\nIdentify the wall construction and how the installer will reach and maintain the sign.\n\n### Review exposure and components\n\nTell us the destination and whether the sign is exposed to rain. Component selection and required documentation must suit the agreed configuration.\n\n### Confirm the light pattern\n\nApprove a drawing showing letter profiles and light-point positions, together with the finish and cable arrangement.\n\n## Make It Your Own\n\nChange the lettering, finish and light-point arrangement. The design can be adapted for a smaller interior feature or a larger entrance identity.\n\nInclude any dimming, replacement-access or event-use requirements at the enquiry stage so they can be reviewed in the quotation."}','$.v'),char(13),'');
